  reduces cardiovascular events in patients with acute coronary syndrome", "abstract": "AIMS Influenza infection has    
  been shown to accentuate the progression of atherosclerosis and precipitate the occurrence of acute coronary          
  syndrome (ACS). However, the protective effects of the influenza vaccine on cardiovascular events are still           
  inconclusive. METHODS AND RESULTS The study was a prospective randomized open with blinded endpoint (PROBE) study.    
