  3:1), with all participants receiving 23-valent-pneumococcal polysaccharide vaccine unless already administered. The  
  primary analysis was the frequency of influenza as recorded by a GP diagnosis of pneumonia or influenza like          
  illness. In 2000, the UK vaccination policy was changed with influenza vaccine becoming available for all people      
  aged 65 years and over irrespective of risk. As a consequence of this policy change, the study had to be              
